/-!
# The chart dictionary for the forms of the complement of the zero section

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes, `L` an invertible `𝒪_X`-module and `L^⋆ ⟶ X` the
complement of the zero section of the associated line bundle. Over an affine open `U` of `X`
the inverse image `π⁻¹U` of `U` in `L^⋆` is again affine, so the sections of the relative
differential forms of `L^⋆` over `π⁻¹U` admit a purely ring-theoretic description: they are the
exterior powers of the Kähler differentials of the ring `Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)` over `Γ(S, V)`, for an
affine open `V` of `S` containing the image.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFormsChartIso`: **the degreewise chart comparison**
  `Γ(Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U) ≅ ⋀^p_{Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)} Γ(Ω_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U)`, the instance at `L^⋆` of
  Tags 01I8 and 01CI on an affine open of an arbitrary scheme.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv`:
  `Ω[Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)⁄Γ(S, V)] ≃ₗ Γ(Ω_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U)`, the instance at `L^⋆` of Tag 01UT, carried
  onto the construction of `Ω` that the graded forms are built from.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFormsKaehlerEquiv`: **the two composed**,
  `Γ(Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U) ≃ₗ ⋀^p_{Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)} Ω[Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)⁄Γ(S, V)]`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferentialsSectionsEquiv`,
  `Situation.laurentUniversalD` and `Situation.laurentGeneratorSections`: the spelling bridges
  the above are assembled from — the sections of the development's two constructions of
  `Ω_{L^⋆/S}`, the universal relative derivation, and the degree-one generator of the exterior
  algebra as a linear map on sections.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearEquivOfIso`: isomorphic `𝒪_X`-modules have
  linearly isomorphic sections over every open. This generalizes
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsTopLinearEquivOfIso`, the case `W = ⊤`, and
  subsumes it.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.differentialsSectionsEquiv`,
  `Scheme.Hom.universalDSections`, `Scheme.Hom.kaehlerChartEquiv`: **the chart dictionary for an
  arbitrary morphism of schemes** — the three items above it with `L^⋆ ⟶ S` replaced by any
  `f : X ⟶ S` and the affineness of the chart supplied as an argument. The `L^⋆` forms are their
  instances at `Situation.laurentToBase`; the generality is needed on `X` itself, and it is a
  restatement rather than new mathematics, the inputs
  `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv` and `cotangentSectionsEquiv_D` already holding for an
  arbitrary morphism.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf`: **`F ≅ ⋀¹ F`** for a sheaf of
  modules on a scheme, with `exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf_hom` naming its forward map as the
  degree-one generator `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator`. The reverse
  isomorphism is `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPowerOneIsoSelf`; what this pair adds
  is the identification of the forward map with the generator, which is what a statement about
  the generator can be transported along.

## Main results

* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.isAffineOpen_laurentPreimage`: **the inverse image of an affine
  open of `X` in `L^⋆` is an affine open**, the projection being affine. This is the hypothesis
  every ring-level description of the forms over `π⁻¹U` is gated on.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferential_add`,
  `Situation.laurentDifferential_mul` and `Situation.laurentDifferential_one`: **the relative de
  Rham differential of `L^⋆` is a derivation** — additive, Leibniz, and killing `1`. Before this
  file the only lemma about `Situation.laurentDifferential` was its compatibility with
  restriction, `Situation.laurentDifferential_map`.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv_D`: **the chart comparison carries
  `KaehlerDifferential.D` to the relative de Rham differential.**
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerChartEquiv_D` and
  `Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top`: **the chart comparison carries the Kähler
  differential to the universal relative derivation, and the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an affine
  chart are generated by the differentials of the functions there** — for an arbitrary morphism.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv_D` and
  `Situation.span_range_universalRelativeDerivation_eq_top`: the two previous items at `L^⋆`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator_sections_surjective`: **the degree-one
  generator of the exterior algebra of a sheaf of modules on a scheme is surjective on sections
  over every open**, nothing being divided out in degree one.
* `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentGeneratorSections_surjective` and
  `Situation.span_range_laurentDifferential_eq_top`: **the sections of `Ω^1_{L^⋆/S}` over the
  chart are generated by the relative de Rham differentials of the functions there**, the
  previous item one degree up. The differential is the universal relative derivation followed by
  the degree-one generator, and the generator is surjective, so the span of its range is the
  image of the span of the derivation's range.

## Implementation notes

What this file provides is the comparison of *modules of sections*, in each degree separately
and over one open at a time, together with the generation statements for `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` and for
`Ω^1_{L^⋆/S}`. What it does not provide is the wedge comparison, identifying
`SheafOfModules.GradedAlgebra.mul` with the product of exterior powers.

The degree-one generator has its target declared at the
`SheafOfModules (Stacks.RingedSpace.structureRingSheaf _)` indexing, while
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearEquivOfIso` reads a morphism at `Y.Modules`. The
two types are equal by definition and still present different instance problems, so the `IsIso`
form `SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.isIso_exteriorGenerator` cannot be consumed
here. What crosses is re-seating the *objects* rather than bridging the morphism:
`exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf` ascribes the bundle's
`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.exteriorGeneratorIso` to the target
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower F 1`, whose own declared type is `X.Modules`, and
definitional unfolding accepts the ascription. Two further pins are needed downstream:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap` has to be given `N := exteriorPower F 1`
  explicitly. Left to unification it takes the generator's own indexing, and the statement then
  elaborates but is not type-correct at `implicit` transparency, so no rewrite fires inside it;
* a span of differentials has to be written through `id (α := Γ(·, ·))`, for the reason the next
  paragraph records: a type ascription does not move the term, instance search reading its
  inferred type and not the ascription.

The scalar action on the sections of a module over an open is available at the `Γ(M, U)`
spelling of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.presheaf`, and *not* at the `M.val.obj (op U)`
spelling in which `Situation.laurentDifferential` is declared: instance search does not cross
between them. The Leibniz rule is therefore stated with `Γ`, and proved by pushing the
derivation's own `PresheafOfModules.Derivation.d_mul` through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap`, the degree-one generator of the exterior
algebra read as a `Γ(L^⋆, V)`-linear map on sections. Taking the generator as a bundled linear
map is what makes `map_smul` available over the ring the statement names.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01CI](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01CI)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01I8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01I8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0FU9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0FU9)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory TopologicalSpace AlgebraicGeometry Opposite

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

/-- **Isomorphic `𝒪_X`-modules have linearly isomorphic sections over every open.** This
generalizes `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.sectionsTopLinearEquivOfIso`, which is the case
`W = ⊤`, and subsumes it: the body is the same with the open as a parameter. -/
def sectionsLinearEquivOfIso {Y : Scheme.{u}} {M N : Y.Modules} (e : M ≅ N)
    (W : Y.Opens) : Γ(M, W) ≃ₗ[Γ(Y, W)] Γ(N, W) :=
  LinearEquiv.ofLinear
    (sectionsLinearMap e.hom W)
    (sectionsLinearMap e.inv W)
    (LinearMap.ext fun x => by
      change e.hom.app W (e.inv.app W x) = x
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, Iso.inv_hom_id,
        Scheme.Modules.Hom.id_app]
      rfl)
    (LinearMap.ext fun x => by
      change e.inv.app W (e.hom.app W x) = x
      rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Scheme.Modules.Hom.comp_app, Iso.hom_inv_id,
        Scheme.Modules.Hom.id_app]
      rfl)

/-- The forward map of `Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearEquivOfIso` is the isomorphism on
sections. -/
theorem sectionsLinearEquivOfIso_apply {Y : Scheme.{u}} {M N : Y.Modules}
    (e : M ≅ N) (W : Y.Opens) (x : Γ(M, W)) :
    sectionsLinearEquivOfIso e W x = e.hom.app W x :=
  rfl

/-! ### The degree-one exterior power of a module on a scheme -/

/-- **`F ≅ ⋀¹ F` for a sheaf of modules on a scheme**: the exterior algebra divides nothing out
in degree one. This is
`SheafOfModules.TensorExteriorSymmetricAlgebras.exteriorGeneratorIso` of the bundle
`SheafOfModules.algebras` that `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower` is defined from,
with its target read at `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPower F 1`, whose declared type
is `X.Modules`. The reverse isomorphism is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.exteriorPowerOneIsoSelf`; what this one carries, and what the
generation statements below consume, is `exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf_hom`. -/
def exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) : F ≅ exteriorPower F 1 :=
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ F).exteriorGeneratorIso

/-- **The identification `F ≅ ⋀¹ F` is the degree-one generator of the exterior algebra.** -/
theorem exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf_hom {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) :
    (exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf F).hom = exteriorGenerator F :=
  (_root_.SheafOfModules.algebras _ F).exteriorGeneratorIso_hom

/-- **The degree-one generator of the exterior algebra is surjective on sections over every
open**, being an isomorphism of sheaves of modules. The implicit degree-one piece is named
`exteriorPower F 1` rather than left to unification, so that the statement is type-correct at
`implicit` transparency and rewrites fire inside it. -/
theorem exteriorGenerator_sections_surjective {X : Scheme.{u}} (F : X.Modules) (W : X.Opens) :
    Function.Surjective
      (sectionsLinearMap (N := exteriorPower F 1) (exteriorGenerator F) W) := fun y => by
  obtain ⟨x, hx⟩ := (sectionsLinearEquivOfIso (exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf F) W).surjective y
  refine ⟨x, ?_⟩
  rw [sectionsLinearMap_apply, ← exteriorGeneratorIsoSelf_hom F]
  exact hx

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)

/-! ### The chart dictionary for an arbitrary morphism

Everything in this section is the chart dictionary of the file's title with `L^⋆ ⟶ S` replaced by
an arbitrary morphism and the affineness of the chart supplied as an argument. Its inputs,
`Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv` and `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv_D`, already hold
in that generality, so this is a restatement and not new mathematics; the `L^⋆` forms below are
its instances at `Situation.laurentToBase`. The generality is needed on `X` itself, where the
differential of a function on a smaller affine open has to be expressed through the differentials
of functions on a bigger one. -/

/-- **The two constructions of the sheaf of relative differentials agree on sections** over an
open: `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf`, which Tag 01UT is stated for, against
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials`, which the differential forms are built
from. -/
def differentialsSectionsEquiv (W : X.Opens) :
    Γ(Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf f, W) ≃ₗ[Γ(X, W)] Γ(relativeDifferentials f, W) :=
  Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearEquivOfIso (cotangentSheafIso f).symm W

/-- **The universal relative derivation read on sections** over an open: the map
`d : Γ(X, W) → Γ(Ω_{X/S}, W)`, with its target named at the `Γ` spelling, which is the one
carrying the module structure the spans below are taken over. -/
def universalDSections (W : X.Opens) : Γ(X, W) →+ Γ(relativeDifferentials f, W) :=
  (universalRelativeDerivation f).d

/-- **The chart comparison** `Ω[Γ(X, U)⁄Γ(S, V)] ≃ₗ Γ(Ω_{X/S}, U)` for an affine open `U` of `X`
mapping into an affine open `V` of `S`: Tag 01UT carried from `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf` onto
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials`. -/
def kaehlerChartEquiv {U : X.Opens} {V : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) (hV : IsAffineOpen V)
    (hUV : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V) :
    letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
    Ω[Γ(X, U)⁄Γ(S, V)] ≃ₗ[Γ(X, U)] Γ(relativeDifferentials f, U) :=
  letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
  (Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv f hU hV hUV).trans (differentialsSectionsEquiv f U)

/-- **The chart comparison carries the Kähler differential to the universal relative
derivation.** -/
theorem kaehlerChartEquiv_D {U : X.Opens} {V : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hUV : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V) (a : Γ(X, U)) :
    letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
    kaehlerChartEquiv f hU hV hUV (KaehlerDifferential.D Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U) a) =
      universalDSections f U a := by
  let := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
  refine Eq.trans (congrArg (differentialsSectionsEquiv f U)
    (Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv_D f hU hV hUV a)) ?_
  exact PresheafOfModulesOfCommRing.Derivation.congr_d
    (universalDerivation_postcomp_ofCotangentSheaf f) a

/-- **The sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over an affine chart are generated by the differentials of the
functions there.** -/
theorem span_range_universalDSections_eq_top {U : X.Opens} {V : S.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U)
    (hV : IsAffineOpen V) (hUV : U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V) :
    Submodule.span Γ(X, U) (Set.range (universalDSections f U)) = ⊤ := by
  let := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE f hUV
  refine Submodule.eq_top_iff'.mpr fun x => ?_
  obtain ⟨y, rfl⟩ := (kaehlerChartEquiv f hU hV hUV).surjective x
  have hy : y ∈ Submodule.span Γ(X, U)
      (Set.range (KaehlerDifferential.D Γ(S, V) Γ(X, U))) := by
    rw [KaehlerDifferential.span_range_derivation]
    trivial
  induction hy using Submodule.span_induction with
  | mem z hz =>
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := hz
      exact Submodule.subset_span ⟨a, (kaehlerChartEquiv_D f hU hV hUV a).symm⟩
  | zero => rw [map_zero]; exact Submodule.zero_mem _
  | add z w _ _ hz hw => rw [map_add]; exact Submodule.add_mem _ hz hw
  | smul r z _ hz => rw [map_smul]; exact Submodule.smul_mem _ r hz

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

namespace Stacks.LineBundle

variable (D : Situation.{u})

/-! ### The chart is affine -/

/-! ### The relative differential of `L^⋆` is a derivation -/

/-- **The universal relative derivation of `L^⋆` over the base, read on sections** over an open
of `L^⋆`: the map `d : Γ(L^⋆, V) → Γ(Ω_{L^⋆/S}, V)`. This is
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation` with its target named at the `Γ`
spelling, which is the one carrying the module structure the spans below are taken over. -/
def Situation.laurentUniversalD (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens) :
    Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, V) →+
      Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase, V) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalDSections D.laurentToBase V

/-- The degree-one generator of the exterior algebra of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}`, read over an open of `L^⋆`
as a linear map on sections. This is the second factor of
`Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentDifferential`, bundled so that its linearity is available
over the ring the statements below name. -/
def Situation.laurentGeneratorSections (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens) :
    Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase, V) →ₗ[
        Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, V)]
      Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V) :=
  Scheme.Modules.sectionsLinearMap
    (N := D.laurentForms 1)
    (Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase)) V

/-- The relative de Rham differential of a function on `L^⋆` is the universal relative
derivation followed by `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentGeneratorSections`. -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferential_eq_generatorSections (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens)
    (b : Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, V)) :
    (D.laurentDifferential V b : Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) =
      D.laurentGeneratorSections V
        ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation D.laurentToBase).d b) :=
  rfl

/-- **The relative de Rham differential of `L^⋆` is additive.** -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferential_add (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens)
    (b c : Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, V)) :
    (D.laurentDifferential V (b + c) : Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) =
      D.laurentDifferential V b + D.laurentDifferential V c :=
  (congrArg (D.laurentGeneratorSections V)
    (map_add
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation D.laurentToBase).d b c)).trans
    (map_add (D.laurentGeneratorSections V) _ _)

/-- **The relative de Rham differential of `L^⋆` kills the constant function `1`.** -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferential_one (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens) :
    (D.laurentDifferential V 1 : Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) = 0 :=
  (congrArg (D.laurentGeneratorSections V)
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation
      D.laurentToBase).d_one (op V))).trans (map_zero (D.laurentGeneratorSections V))

/-- **The Leibniz rule for the relative de Rham differential of `L^⋆`**:
`d (b c) = b d c + c d b` for functions `b` and `c` on an open of `L^⋆`. This is what terminates
the expansion of a homogeneous form over a basic open into forms restricted from the ambient
affine open. -/
theorem Situation.laurentDifferential_mul (V : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens)
    (b c : Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, V)) :
    (D.laurentDifferential V (b * c) : Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) =
      b • id (α := Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) (D.laurentDifferential V c) +
        c • id (α := Γ(D.laurentForms 1, V)) (D.laurentDifferential V b) :=
  (congrArg (D.laurentGeneratorSections V)
    ((AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.universalRelativeDerivation
      D.laurentToBase).d_mul b c)).trans
    ((map_add (D.laurentGeneratorSections V) _ _).trans
      (congrArg₂ (· + ·) (map_smul (D.laurentGeneratorSections V) b _)
        (map_smul (D.laurentGeneratorSections V) c _)))

/-! ### The degreewise chart comparison -/

/-- **The sections of `Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` over the inverse image of an affine open `U` of `X` are the
`p`th exterior power of the sections of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` there**:

`Γ(Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U) ≅ ⋀^p_{Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)} Γ(Ω_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U)`.

This is Tags 01I8 and 01CI, in the form
`Stacks.AffineExteriorPower.affineOpenExteriorPowerΓIso` states them for an affine open of an
arbitrary scheme, instantiated at the structure morphism `L^⋆ ⟶ S` and the affine open `π⁻¹U`
of `L^⋆`. It is the degreewise half of the chart dictionary; the de Rham differential is not
transported by it. -/
def Situation.laurentFormsChartIso (U : D.X.affineOpens) (p : ℕ) :
    ModuleCat.of Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
        Γ(D.laurentForms (p : ℤ), D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) ≅
      ModuleCat.of Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
        (⋀[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)]^p
          Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase,
            D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) :=
  haveI : (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials
      D.laurentToBase).IsQuasicoherent :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isQuasicoherent_relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase
  Stacks.AffineExteriorPower.affineOpenExteriorPowerΓIso
    (X := D.laurentSpectrum) (U := D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
    (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase)
    (D.isAffineOpen_laurentPreimage U.2)
    (Scheme.Modules.isExteriorAlgebra_exteriorAlgebra
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase)) p

/-! ### The Kähler differentials of the chart -/

/-- **The two constructions of the sheaf of relative differentials of `L^⋆` agree on sections**
over an open of `L^⋆`: this reads `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.cotangentSheafIso` — the
comparison of `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf`, which Tag 01UT is stated for, with
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials`, which the graded forms of `L^⋆` are built
from — as a linear equivalence over the ring of functions on that open. -/
def Situation.laurentDifferentialsSectionsEquiv (W : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens) :
    Γ(Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf D.laurentToBase, W) ≃ₗ[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, W)]
      Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase, W) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.differentialsSectionsEquiv D.laurentToBase W

/-- **The sections of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` over the inverse image of an affine open `U` of `X` are the
Kähler differentials of the ring of functions there**:

`Ω[Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)⁄Γ(S, V)] ≃ₗ Γ(Ω_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U)`,

for an affine open `V` of `S` with `π⁻¹U` mapping into it. This is Tag 01UT, in the form
`Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSectionsEquiv` states it, instantiated at the structure morphism
`L^⋆ ⟶ S`, and then carried from `Stacks.Smooth.cotangentSheaf` onto
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials` — the construction of `Ω` the graded forms
of `L^⋆` are built from — along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.cotangentSheafIso`. -/
def Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv (U : D.X.affineOpens) (V : D.S.affineOpens)
    (hUV : D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ D.laurentToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) :
    letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE D.laurentToBase hUV
    Ω[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)⁄Γ(D.S, V.1)]
        ≃ₗ[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)]
      Γ(AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.relativeDifferentials D.laurentToBase,
        D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerChartEquiv D.laurentToBase
    (D.isAffineOpen_laurentPreimage U.2) V.2 hUV

/-- **The chart dictionary for the forms of `L^⋆`, degreewise**: over the inverse image of an
affine open `U` of `X` mapping into an affine open `V` of `S`, the sections of
`Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}` are the `p`th exterior power of the Kähler differentials of `Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)` over
`Γ(S, V)`:

`Γ(Ω^p_{L^⋆/S}, π⁻¹U) ≃ₗ ⋀^p_{Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)} Ω[Γ(L^⋆, π⁻¹U)⁄Γ(S, V)]`.

This is the composite of `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentFormsChartIso` with the `p`th
exterior power of `Stacks.LineBundle.Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv`. It translates a
*section* of the sheaf-level forms into a ring-level form; it does **not** transport the de Rham
differential, and it is stated for one open at a time, so it carries no compatibility with
restriction to a smaller open. -/
def Situation.laurentFormsKaehlerEquiv (U : D.X.affineOpens) (V : D.S.affineOpens)
    (hUV : D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ D.laurentToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) (p : ℕ) :
    letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE D.laurentToBase hUV
    Γ(D.laurentForms (p : ℤ), D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
        ≃ₗ[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)]
      ⋀[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)]^p
        Ω[Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)⁄Γ(D.S, V.1)] :=
  letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE D.laurentToBase hUV
  (D.laurentFormsChartIso U p).toLinearEquiv.trans
    (Stacks.AffineExteriorPower.exteriorPowerCongr
      (D.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv U V hUV).symm p)

/-! ### The chart differentials generate -/

/-- **The chart dictionary carries the Kähler differential to the relative de Rham
differential.** This is the only compatibility with the differential the characterization of
the graded pieces needs: not that the dictionary *is* the differential, but that the two have
the same image, which this identity gives pointwise. -/
theorem Situation.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv_D (U : D.X.affineOpens) (V : D.S.affineOpens)
    (hUV : D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ D.laurentToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V.1)
    (a : Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) :
    letI := Stacks.Smooth.algebraAppLE D.laurentToBase hUV
    D.laurentKaehlerChartEquiv U V hUV
        (KaehlerDifferential.D Γ(D.S, V.1)
          Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) a) =
      D.laurentUniversalD (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) a :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerChartEquiv_D D.laurentToBase
    (D.isAffineOpen_laurentPreimage U.2) V.2 hUV a

/-- **The sections of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` over the chart are generated by the differentials of the
functions there.** This is the statement that terminates the expansion of a homogeneous form
over a smaller affine open: combined with quasi-coherence of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}`, which gives that the
sections over `π⁻¹W` are generated by restrictions from `π⁻¹U`, it says that every differential
over `π⁻¹W` is a combination of differentials of functions restricted from `π⁻¹U`. -/
theorem Situation.span_range_universalRelativeDerivation_eq_top (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    (V : D.S.affineOpens)
    (hUV : D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ D.laurentToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) :
    Submodule.span Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
        (Set.range (D.laurentUniversalD (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))) = ⊤ :=
  AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.span_range_universalDSections_eq_top D.laurentToBase
    (D.isAffineOpen_laurentPreimage U.2) V.2 hUV

/-- **The degree-one generator of the exterior algebra of `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` is surjective on sections**
over every open of `L^⋆`. This is the second factor of `Situation.laurentDifferential`, so it is
what carries the generation statement for `Ω_{L^⋆/S}` one degree up. -/
theorem Situation.laurentGeneratorSections_surjective (W : D.laurentSpectrum.Opens) :
    Function.Surjective (D.laurentGeneratorSections W) :=
  Scheme.Modules.exteriorGenerator_sections_surjective _ W

/-- **The sections of `Ω^1_{L^⋆/S}` over the chart are generated by the relative de Rham
differentials of the functions there.** The differential is the universal relative derivation
followed by the degree-one generator of the exterior algebra; the derivation's range spans by
`Situation.span_range_universalRelativeDerivation_eq_top` and the generator is surjective on
sections, so the span of the differentials is the image of a span that is everything.

This is the chart-level generation statement for `Ω^1_{L^⋆/S}`, and it stands on its own. It is
*not* what the descent of a homogeneous form to a smaller affine chart runs through: that
expansion terminates at `Situation.laurentDifferential_pullback_mem_span` of
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.DeRham.LineBundle.LaurentPullbackDifferential`, which is stated
about a *pulled-back* function over the smaller chart and is what
`Situation.isHomogeneousLaurentForm_mem_span` actually consumes. This file is not in the import
closure of that descent, so nothing here is on the critical path of Tag 0FUH clause (1). -/
theorem Situation.span_range_laurentDifferential_eq_top (U : D.X.affineOpens)
    (V : D.S.affineOpens)
    (hUV : D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1 ≤ D.laurentToBase ⁻¹ᵁ V.1) :
    Submodule.span Γ(D.laurentSpectrum, D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)
        (Set.range fun b => id (α := Γ(D.laurentForms 1,
            D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
          (D.laurentDifferential (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) b)) = ⊤ := by
  have hrange : (Set.range fun b => id (α := Γ(D.laurentForms 1,
        D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1))
        (D.laurentDifferential (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) b)) =
      D.laurentGeneratorSections (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1) ''
        Set.range (D.laurentUniversalD (D.laurentSpectrumToBase ⁻¹ᵁ U.1)) := by
    rw [← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  rw [hrange, Submodule.span_image,
    D.span_range_universalRelativeDerivation_eq_top U V hUV, Submodule.map_top,
    LinearMap.range_eq_top]
  exact D.laurentGeneratorSections_surjective _

end Stacks.LineBundle

end
